    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95428.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 23,
    "turn_text": "Maybe I won't cry this time. I should be embarrassing in front of you. My second point is that I think there is more agreement in the Democratic Party than people do realize. Sure, we are having some disagreements. But I think once people took a look at the battle plan, they saw a lot of things that they liked. And to me, it's another example that people need to talk to each other. And I hope that people won't make snap judgments and run to social media right away because that's where you can get into trouble. The third point I wanted to make is I think it shows it's okay to admit a mistake, to evolve, and to move forward. You know, battles change on the no fossil fuel pledge. makes me respect him more. And I think Varshney showed more maturity as a 25 year old than most of the Republican caucus on climate. They can't admit that they've made a mistake on climate denialism and we're stuck.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_02",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
