    "turn_idx": 70,
    "turn_text": "To me, it seems like the easiest way to go, because even if you make your building zero emissions, you still have to deal with the generation resource. It's not like the emissions just go away. But when you look at our national energy mix, you're talking about seven percent renewables. If you don't count hydro, I think close to 13 or 14 percent, if you do count hydro, that's going to take time. But changing out appliances, making your buildings more efficient, that's something people do every day. That's something that I think when someone says, I don't go, well, that's unachievable. You're being insane. That's something you could do tomorrow if you just put the money forward.",
