    "turn_text": "I hear that and I hear that line a lot that this is an opportunity for people who work in unions. I mean, I actually don't know the numbers on that. What is the meat around that? We should have someone on from a union to really tell us their perspective because I don't want to just accept that as necessarily true because this is an emerging industry, the clean energy industry. And it is noted that some of those jobs don't pay as well as fossil fuel jobs did. So that's just a reality. So I think we actually should really flesh out that conversation. I'm just gonna put a pin in that one. I think similarly on this 100% discussion, I think it'll be interesting to see if Biden does take the no fossil fuel money pledge because that's something that upset unions when the Democratic National Committee did it when they swore off fossil fuel corporation money and unions were the ones to push back then and the Democratic National Committee actually ended up reversing course and decided to take that fossil fuel money once more. So the Biden story thinks it'll be a really interesting one to watch and it'll say a lot about where Democratic voters overall kind of sit today.",
