    "turn_text": "Well, you started off by saying this was the first meaningful climate legislation in 10 years, and that's right. So this was a very important statement for Democrats to make early in the term now that the House of Representatives is in democratic control. This is one of our priorities. And if you think back to what's happened in the last 10 years, while we've made progress, boy, the science is in now, the administration's own fourth climate assessment says we do not have very long to act to cut carbon pollution before the worst impacts of climate change are cells. I mean, people are already feeling the impacts of climate personally. I mean, my own family a year and a half ago is that monster hurricane Irma loomed out off the coast of Florida. We had to pack up bar belonging. My most cherished pictures and everything. I drove them to the top of the parking garage and we had to get out of town because of The Tampa Bay area is the worst, the most vulnerable to storm surge, but we were lucky because we had time to get out of the way. If the wildfires are moving so quickly, much more intense. Look at the floods and the heartland and the important ag areas. We just don't have time to waste. So it was a good first step, climate action now, but now we must move on to a bolder climate action.",
