    "turn_idx": 120,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, to your point, Shane, I don't think we can say that international climate policy isn't getting ratified because Democrats don't want it to. I think there is strong pushback on the Republicans' eye to have such a vote and it probably would not pass, and so Democrats found other avenues. But to why the amendment in the House didn't pass just recently, that probably has to do with the politics. Similar to Republicans taking an up or down vote on whether or not climate's real, Democrats probably don't want to have a vote saying that the previous pathway they pursued on climate, the regulatory pathway, was the wrong way to go. So these are some of the political questions at play.",
