    "turn_idx": 127,
    "turn_text": "You mentioned the first bill, an earlier bill that House Democrats did pass was around campaign finance reform. And Representative Caster mentions that in our interview. She talks about too much dark money in politics and points to the fossil fuel industry, which is interesting given our conversation around Beto and the no fossil fuel money pledge. Brandon, I'm curious to you, you know, our Democrats just moving away from fossil fuel money. They're sort of like, this is just not something, it's not very compelling to us. Democrats historically have not made all that much of their money from the fossil fuel industry. So do you think this is going to be an ongoing tension around whether or not to accept those donations or are Democrats swearing off of fossil fuel money altogether? And this is just a matter of time.",
