    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/5/95428.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 136,
    "turn_text": "I wanted to say something nice about Chairman Murkowski. She introduced a bipartisan bill. This is super nerdy on the supply chain for lithium ion batteries. We need batteries for energy storage and for our electric vehicles. Now, what's going to be the winning technology on those batteries? I don't know. But what we know right now is lithium ion works. The costs are coming down. But in order to build those batteries, we need certain rare minerals to do it. And right now, China's got most of it. And so she introduced a bill called the American Mineral Security Act, which would help protect and secure the supply chain to produce these lithium ion batteries. So super wonky, nerdy issue, but super critical. And I'm happy that Chairman Murkowski is taking leadership on this.",
